 {
  "section": "Platform & tooling",
  "key": "Y2",
  "title": "Three loose ends: a repeated read, a missing time, and code nothing uses",
  "sub": "Each carries a recommendation; nothing here blocks anything that shipped.",
  "dims": [
   "Reliability Low–Med",
   "Size S each",
   "Codex 0–1 each",
   "Touches data: one of the three needs a one-time cleanup you run"
  ],
  "pop": "Advisors’ screens, a restored line’s note, and some code nothing uses.",
  "styles": [],
  "blocks": [
   "<figure class=\"viz\">\n        <figcaption class=\"viz-cap\"><span>Three small calls</span><span class=\"hint\">scroll &rarr;</span></figcaption>\n        <div class=\"scroller\">\n          <table class=\"plain\">\n            <thead>\n              <tr><th scope=\"col\">Loose end</th><th scope=\"col\">Recommendation</th></tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"surface-name\">Every advisor screen re-reads every customer question ever asked &mdash; answered ones included &mdash; every 15 seconds, and picks out the open ones afterwards. Fine today; the cost grows with every question a store ever asks. Narrowing it to open questions needs a one-time cleanup you run on the older questions.</td>\n                <td><span class=\"gate good\">fix now, while the cleanup is small</span></td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"surface-name\">A restored line&rsquo;s note can&rsquo;t say who decided or when &mdash; the app keeps one answer time per RO, overwritten by each reply, not one per line. The per-part verbal OK on the parts page records no customer time at all.</td>\n                <td><span class=\"gate warn\">later &mdash; only the restore note wants it</span></td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"surface-name\">Since the one-card redo of video uploads, nothing on screen uses the older &ldquo;an earlier video failed &mdash; Retry / Discard&rdquo; pieces; they live on only in tests. The written rules for a safe discard already live in the lessons doc.</td>\n                <td><span class=\"gate good\">delete them; the written rules stay</span></td>\n              </tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n      </figure>"
  ],
  "questions": [
   [
    "",
    "Take the three recommendations as a block, or pull any one out?"
   ]
  ],
  "ruled": []
 },
 {
